    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d273">

                <pb facs="0367" n="265" xml:id="pg265"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94 Advisory Committee/29: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Switzerland
                        (Wilson), at Geneva</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-03-31T18:00:00-05:00">March 31, 1933—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>92. Your 159, March 29, 11 a.m. I desire absolutely to avoid being drawn into any
                    discussion of this Government’s attitude with regard to any proposed embargo on
                    export of arms until the League shall have made its own decision. I do not
                    intend that this Government shall assume the role of mentor to the League or
                    accept a responsibility which initially lies with and belongs to the League
                    under the League’s Covenant. You should, by refusing to be drawn into discussion
                    of the subject of embargoes, discourage any hope or expectation on the part of
                    the League to the contrary.</p>
                <p>Please review Department’s 2, September 23, 1932, noon,<anchor n="85"
                        xml:id="d273-f1"/> first two paragraphs, and Department’s 85, March 11,
                    1933, 7 p.m., and 89, March 16, 1933, 8 p.m.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
